  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "F89-01",
      "severity": "metric_wording",
      "finding": "The valid fuzzer records the count of expected printed values using lines += len(exp); it compares got = stdout.decode(...).split(), so output equality is whitespace-token equality, NOT strict newline or byte-for-byte equality. Zero failures remains useful numeric-output evidence, but 'output lines compared' is imprecise."
    },
    {
      "id": "F89-02",
      "severity": "coverage_overstatement",
      "finding": "shape(prog) tallies every generated function definition using prog[0], and histogram updates before execution. It does not count confirmed dynamic calls; the 27–40-variable bins represent 20,398 generated function definitions, not 20,398 proven executed call frames."
    },
    {
      "id": "F89-03",
      "severity": "exit_validation_gap",
      "finding": "Generated binary returncode is tested only for negative (signal) exit. A positive nonzero exit code can be classified as ok if stdout whitespace tokens equal expected; recommend requiring rr.returncode == 0."
    },
    {
      "id": "F89-04",
      "severity": "independent_rerun_provenance",
      "finding": "R17 final, R17 no-workarounds and R18 valid summary file Git blobs are byte-identical. Identical deterministic summaries are compatible with repeated runs but do not prove distinct run executions. Neither file provides per-program transcripts to audit the 388,616 count from raw outputs."
    },
    {
      "id": "F89-05",
      "severity": "scope",
      "finding": "The generator deliberately avoids floats, strings, side-effecting functions, division by zero, out-of-bounds indices, language packs, and Windows. The sample cannot establish universal correctness."
    }
  ],
